[IQ Generator Preset]
# Lesson 13: differential QPSK under a carrier offset.
# DQPSK carries the data in the phase change between consecutive symbols, not in the absolute phase. A 5 Hz carrier offset spins the whole constellation (matched-filter view), but each symbol-to-symbol step stays within a few degrees of the transmitted 0, 90, 180 or 270 degrees. That is why a differential receiver needs no carrier-phase recovery, at the price of a noise penalty of a couple of dB compared with coherent QPSK. Set CFO to 0 and compare the constellation.
Version=3
Modulation=DQPSK
NumberOfSymbols=1024
SymbolRateBaud=1000
SamplesPerSymbol=8
Pulse=RRC
RRCBeta=0.2
SpanSymbols=10
AmplitudeGain=1
DataSource=Random
Seed=5489
Bits=
